# EventFlow – Architecture

## Architecture Style

EventFlow is implemented as a **modular monolithic backend**.

### Why Monolith First
- Faster development and iteration
- Easier debugging and tracing
- Clear ownership of transactions
- Avoids premature distributed complexity

The system is designed so that individual modules can later be extracted into microservices if needed.

## High-Level Layers

1. Controller Layer
   - Handles HTTP requests and responses
   - Performs request validation
   - No business logic

2. Service Layer
   - Contains core business logic
   - Manages transactions
   - Enforces business rules

3. Repository Layer
   - Handles database access
   - Uses JPA abstractions

4. Domain Layer
   - Core entities (Event, Booking)
   - Represents business state

## Technology Choices

- Java 17
- Spring Boot
- Maven
- PostgreSQL (planned)
- JPA / Hibernate
